## Location
- /Volumes/Attic/Desktop/Projects/crates/schc/src/fragment/ack_always.rs lines 15, 55, 302

## Problem
```rust
const MAX_PACKET_SIZE: usize = 1280;

pub struct Sender<...> {
    packet: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],
    // ...
}

pub struct Receiver<...> {
    buffer: [u8; MAX_PACKET_SIZE],
    // ...
}
```

The buffer size is hardcoded and not exposed as a const generic or configuration option.

## API Risk
1. Memory waste: A sender fragmenting a 50-byte packet still allocates 1280 bytes
2. Size limit: Packets larger than 1280 bytes cannot be fragmented
3. Inconsistency: `AckOnErrorReceiver` takes a user-provided buffer (`&'a mut [u8]`), giving the caller control

## Suggested Fix
Match the AckOnError pattern - take storage as a parameter:
```rust
pub struct Sender<'a, const M: u8, const N: u8, const T: u8, const TILE: usize> {
    packet: &'a [u8],
    // ...
}
```

Or add MAX_PACKET_SIZE as another const generic.
